    {
      "id": "claim_517a5715ece54e8b889f926b8e282f58",
      "statement": "safety_gate derives scrubbed, token-bounded history views from checkpointed messages, then resets all per-turn downstream state channels (retrievals, merged, evaluation, gap_round/gap_pending/gap_filled, generation, validated, route/branch fields, error, etc.) before processing the new question, which is essential for a reused checkpointed thread; it writes a scrubbed question/working query, a model-driven safety classification, notices, and either a refusal/direct response or a deterministic route into the retrieval pipeline.",
